---
import ProfilePhoto from './ProfilePhoto.astro';
---

<section class="section relative overflow-hidden">
  <!-- Decorative background elements -->
  <div class="absolute top-5 right-10 w-48 h-48 border border-amber-400/15 rounded-full opacity-40 blur-sm"></div>
  <div class="absolute -bottom-20 left-0 w-80 h-80 border-2 border-purple-500/10 rounded-full opacity-30 blur-lg"></div>
  <div class="absolute top-1/2 right-1/4 w-1.5 h-1.5 bg-amber-400/50 rounded-full animate-pulse"></div>

  <div class="container-page relative z-10">
    <h2 class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-bold mb-12 text-slate-100">
      About Me
    </h2>
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-12 items-start">
      <!-- Photo -->
      <div class="lg:col-span-1 flex justify-center">
        <ProfilePhoto />
      </div>

      <!-- Text -->
      <div class="lg:col-span-2">
        <div class="space-y-6 text-slate-300 text-lg leading-relaxed">
          <p>
            I design and build production-grade AI systems that bridge enterprise architecture with hands-on engineering. With 14+ years of experience—including 7+ years in AI/ML and cloud—I specialize in developing scalable GenAI and Agentic AI solutions that move from prototypes to real-world, high-impact deployments.
          </p>
          <p>
            Currently working as a Senior AI Architect, I focus on building and deploying LLM-powered systems, including multi-agent workflows, RAG pipelines, and enterprise AI platforms across regulated industries such as Bio-Pharma and Energy. I've led cross-functional teams delivering multiple production-grade GenAI systems and have been recognized with multiple innovation awards.
          </p>
          <p>
            I specialize in Agentic AI, Multi-Agent Systems, RAG, LLM Orchestration, Python, Data Pipelines, AWS/Azure, and Enterprise Architecture. Open for AI Architect / AI Engineering Manager roles in Biopharma, FinServ, or AI-native companies in NJ/NYC or remote-US.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
